      "id": "measuring-distances"
    },
    "summary": "Distances in rules use 2 terms:\n\n- **Within** a distance means no further away than it; a model is within if its base is even partly inside it, and a unit is within if at least 1 of its models is.\n- **Wholly within** means a model’s entire base is inside the distance (for a **FRAME** model, the entire model), and for a unit, that every one of its models is.",
